# {{ company_prog_name }} — Help

Present the map below — write in {{ operator_voice }}: tight, no emoji.
Do NOT run any command to produce it; this is orientation, not a status
check (state is `/cs-review`'s job). Adapt phrasing freely, keep the
content exact.

## What this is

The customer-service operator for **{{ email_address }}**: this session
drives the mrcall-desktop engine (synced mail, relationship memory,
tasks, trained voice). It triages, drafts and advances campaigns;
nothing is sent without the operator's say-so (draft-first; the
autonomy dial is a deliberate later step).

## The commands (you type these)

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `/cs-review` | **the one you type when you sit down.** Settings in force, whether the unattended run is running, every draft with a verdict and its handles, open tasks and escalations, the 45-day support queue with customers separated out{% if producer_adapter != 'none' %}, the day's outreach candidates{% endif %}, what changed in the repo and what is waiting on you |
| `/cs-account <name>` | deep-dive on one account (read-only) |
| `/cs-cron` | the scheduled unattended run: status, install/remove (confirmed), pause/resume |
| `/cs-campaign` | design a new campaign: pack + wiring, draft-first |
| `/cs-help` | this map |

## Or just ask

- *"what's new today?"* / *"what's still open in support mail?"*
- *"load customer X"* (docs + engine memory — before any customer work)
- *"draft a reply to X"* (a DRAFT lands in Gmail Drafts; you send)
- *"I called him, close this one"* (resolved off-email: it gets recorded, so
  the sweep stops re-raising it — reversible)
- *"this one I'm writing myself"* (still open, but yours: nobody else drafts,
  writes or mails them, and it stays on your list with the age — reversible)
- *"find the document about Y"*

Behind those sit the operator skills (`cs-triage-mail`,
`cs-campaign-tick`, `cs-customer`, `cs-find-document`; `cs-operator` is
the headless cron bootstrap) — they fire on their own when the request
matches.

## The hard lines (always true)

- Draft-first: every outgoing mail is reviewed until send mode is
  deliberately enabled (`cs config` says which is in force). Dedup (Gmail
  Sent truth) and the dossier-before-contact rule are not negotiable.
- Kill-switch: `touch ~/.{{ company_slug }}-cs/CS_PAUSE` stops every
  scheduled run; remove the file to resume.

## Deeper

- `CLAUDE.md` — the operator manual (verbs, RPC shapes, pipeline, safety)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — this clone's as-built configuration
- `campaigns/README.md` — what a campaign pack is
- `cs --help` — the CLI, one line per verb
- `cs config` — the settings actually in force and which file declares each
  one (ask it rather than reading `manifest.toml` and the `.env` files)

End by asking what they want to do — and if this looks like the start of
a work session, suggest `/cs-review`.
